- Certificate CN
- SAN/FQDN
- Environment
- Certificate status

MASK:
- Requester personal information where unnecessary
- Any sensitive identifiers


======================================================================
4. CERTIFICATE FILES
======================================================================

After the CMP request was completed, the certificate material was downloaded/received.

During our implementation we worked with files similar to:

Certificate.cer.txt
PrivateKey.key.txt
CertAndKey.pfx

The exact filenames may vary depending on the CMP download/process.

Certificate file:
Contains the public certificate.

Private key:
Contains the private key corresponding to the certificate.

PFX:
A PKCS#12 package that can contain the certificate and private key.

SECURITY NOTE:

Never:

- Paste the private key into Confluence.
- Upload the private key to Confluence.
- Document the private-key password.
- Put passwords directly into shell commands where they remain in shell history.
- Share the private key through email/chat unless an approved Citi process explicitly requires it.


