======================================================================
7. ISSUE ENCOUNTERED DURING PRIVATE-KEY DECRYPTION
======================================================================

Initially the following filename was used:

PrivateKey.key

However, the actual downloaded file was:

PrivateKey.key.txt

This resulted in an OpenSSL error similar to:

Could not open file or uri for loading private key
No such file or directory

Resolution:

Use the exact downloaded filename:

winpty openssl rsa -provider default -provider legacy -in PrivateKey.key.txt -out PrivateKey_decrypted.key


Lesson Learned:

Always verify the downloaded filenames before running the OpenSSL command.

Command:

ls -l


