12. VIP PROFILE CONFIGURATION
======================================================================

Review the profiles associated with the VIP.

Depending on the CAS/NSX configuration, this may include:

- Application profile
- TCP profile
- SSL/TLS profile
- Client SSL profile
- Server SSL profile
- Persistence/profile settings
- Health monitor

IMPORTANT:

Do not change profiles simply because they are visible in CAS.

Only modify the profile required by the approved network design/change.

For our NuraRec setup, the important question is:

"Where does TLS terminate?"

If the VIP is configured as L4 TCP passthrough, the VIP forwards the TCP connection without decrypting HTTPS.

In that architecture:

Client
  |
 HTTPS
  v
WIP
  |
  v
L4 TCP VIP
  |
  | Encrypted TLS connection continues
  v
ECS/OpenShift Ingress/Router
  |
  | TLS termination
  v
Application Service

Therefore, a certificate stored in CAS is not automatically used just because it exists in Certificate Management.

The certificate must be associated with the component/profile that actually terminates TLS.


