======================================================================
17. 504 GATEWAY TIMEOUT TROUBLESHOOTING
======================================================================

A 504 Gateway Timeout does not automatically mean there is a certificate problem.

The complete path should be checked:

APIGEE
   |
   v
WIP
   |
   v
VIP
   |
   v
ECS/OpenShift
   |
   v
Service
   |
   v
Application Pod


Possible causes include:

- WIP pointing/selecting an incorrect VIP
- VIP backend/pool still using an old destination
- Backend unreachable
- Incorrect backend port
- Failed health monitor
- ECS route/service problem
- Application not responding
- Application response exceeding gateway timeout

When a backend/cluster is migrated, verify the backend configuration associated with the existing VIP rather than immediately changing the external WIP endpoint.


