22. KEY TAKEAWAY
======================================================================

The certificate configuration must follow the actual TLS termination architecture.

Creating a certificate in CMP and importing it into CAS does not by itself guarantee that the certificate will be presented to clients.

The complete path must be understood:

APIGEE/Client
      ↓
WIP
      ↓
VIP
      ↓
ECS/OpenShift
      ↓
Application

WIP provides the stable externally known hostname and selects/routes toward the appropriate VIP.

The VIP provides a stable virtual endpoint and allows backend infrastructure to change without requiring upstream consumers to change their endpoint.

The certificate must ultimately be configured/associated at the layer that terminates TLS.

For troubleshooting, always validate the certificate using the actual NuraRec hostname/SNI rather than relying only on a direct VIP-IP test.






